1.8.text:
BY THE GRACE OF ALMIGHTY GOD
THE REGENT OF OGAN KOMERING ULU,

Considering: a. that all forms of violence, especially gender-based violence and violence against children, are violations of human rights and crimes against human dignity as well as forms of discrimination;
b. that victims of gender-based violence and violence against children must receive protection, both from the regional government and/or the community, so as to avoid and be free from violence and/or threats of violence within the scope of the household and the community;
c. that based on Law Number 23 of 2002 concerning Child Protection and Law Number 23 of 2004 concerning the Elimination of Domestic Violence, the Regional Government together with the community is obligated to undertake prevention, protection, and recovery efforts for victims of gender-based violence and violence against children;
d. that based on the considerations as referred to in letters b and c, it is necessary to establish a Regional Regulation of Ogan Komering Ulu Regency concerning the Implementation of Protection for Victims of Gender-Based Violence and Violence Against Children.

In View of: 1. Article 18 paragraph (6) of the 1945 Constitution of the Republic of Indonesia.
